---
title: Vegetarian Shepherd's Pie
description: Indian-spiced lentil and vegetable stew under curried mashed potatoes.
source: https://www.feastingathome.com/vegetarian-shepherds-pie/
author: Sylvia Fountaine (Feasting At Home)
servings: 6
time required: 60 minutes
course: main
cuisine: Indian-inspired
tags:
  - vegetarian
  - lentils
  - shepherd's pie
  - curry
  - make-ahead
  - scaling
---

Preheat the #oven{} to 350°F.

== Potatoes ==

Cut @Yukon gold potatoes{2 1/2%lb}(or other thin-skinned potatoes) into 1-inch slices and place in a #large pot{}. Cover with 1 inch of salted water. Bring to a boil over high heat, then reduce to a simmer over medium-low, cover, and cook until very tender, about ~{20-25%minutes}.

== Lentils ==

Cook @dried lentils{1%cup}(black beluga or French green; not split) in salted boiling water like pasta until al dente, about ~{20-25%minutes}, then drain. You need about @cooked lentils{2 1/2%cups}.

== Filling ==

In a #10-12 inch ovenproof skillet{} (or wide shallow Dutch oven), heat @ghee{2%tbsp}(ghee tastes best; vegan butter also works) over medium-high heat. Sauté @onion{1%large}(diced) until softened, about ~{2-3%minutes}.

Reduce heat to medium. Add @garlic{4%cloves}(roughly chopped) and sauté until fragrant, about ~{2%minutes}. Add @carrot{2%cups}(diced) and @celery{2%cups}(diced); cook until softened, about ~{5-7%minutes}.

Add @salt{1%tsp}, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @ground coriander{1%tsp}, @dried fenugreek leaves{2%tsp}, and @garam masala{2%tsp}.

Add @vegetable broth{1%cup}. Bring to a simmer over medium heat, cover, and cook over medium-low until the carrots are tender, about ~{7-8%minutes}.

== Gravy ==

Meanwhile, in a #small pot{} over medium heat, simmer @cumin seeds{1%tsp} and @fennel seeds{1%tsp} in @ghee{2%tbsp}(or olive oil) until fragrant and golden.

Add @all-purpose flour{3%tbsp}(gluten-free flour works), whisking and toasting for ~{1%minute}. Gradually whisk in warm @vegetable broth{1 1/4%cups}. Cook over medium heat until slightly thickened.

Add the gravy to the filling along with @frozen peas{1%cup} and the drained lentils. Mix to combine. Taste and adjust @kosher salt{}, @black pepper{}, and @garam masala{}. The filling should be a thick, saucy stew — add a splash of broth if dry, or simmer off excess liquid if too watery.

== Mash & Assemble ==

Drain the potatoes (save some hot potato water), return to the pot, and mash with @ghee{4%tbsp}, @plain yogurt{1/2%cup}, and @milk{1/2%cup}(or half-and-half / cream). Loosen with warm potato water if needed. Season with @salt{1%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp}, and @yellow curry powder{1-2%tsp}. Mash until light and fluffy.

Spoon the mashed potatoes over the lentil stew and spread like frosting.

Bake uncovered at 350°F until golden and bubbling, about ~{20-25%minutes}. Optionally brown under the broiler. Garnish with @scallions{}(or chives or cilantro) if desired.
